        "subject": "Run tests from the dashboard: pick cases, adjust test data, edit descriptions",
        "body": "Run tests from the dashboard: pick cases, adjust test data, edit descriptions\n\n- New \"Run tests\" page (#/console): tick the test cases, choose 1-10 rounds\n  and change the test data for this run. \"Run\" starts the workflow through\n  the GitHub API with the owner's fine-grained token (kept in the browser\n  only), then shows the progress, lets you cancel, and shows the result.\n- Workflow inputs `cases` and `params`. run-rounds.mjs checks them with\n  shared/case-params.mjs (the same rules the console uses) and runs only the\n  chosen cases; aggregate.mjs records the selection and the test data used.\n- Default test data and its rules live in config/cases.json; the tests read\n  it through the `data` fixture, so a run can override any value.\n- Titles and descriptions (zh-TW / EN) live in config/descriptions.json and\n  can be edited on the dashboard (each save is a commit through the contents\n  API). {param} placeholders show the test data a run used. The test code is\n  never changed by these edits.\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "NTCloudy",
          "email": "210337045+NTCloudy@users.noreply.github.com",
